77:    \begin{abstract}In this paper, we propose a new method to obtain new permutation polynomials over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$. Using this method, we extend many known permutation polynomials, which take the form $\sum_i(x^q-x+\delta)^{s_i}+L(x)$, where $L(x)$ is a $q$-polynomial over $\mathbb{F}_q$ and $\delta\in\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$. We also present an alternative approach for constructing permutation polynomials of the form $x+\gamma\Tr_q^{q^d}(x^{q+1}+x^{2q+2})$ for the cases where $q=2^m$, $2\nmid d$ and $\Tr_q^{q^d}(x)=x+x^q+\dots+x^{q^{d-1}}$.
